includes:
    - phpstan.neon

# Tracks level 7 as a non-blocking signal, not a gate. OPEN.md already
# records the reason: level 6 is clean, level 7 currently surfaces 483
# findings (mostly |false/|WP_Error unions PHPStan is right to flag but
# this codebase hasn't paid down yet) -- the same "a gate that fails on
# day one gets disabled" reasoning phpcs-changed.sh's own comment already
# applies to WPCS. This file exists so CI can report the count and let it
# trend down over time, without blocking any PR on debt nobody's
# committed to a plan for yet. Reuses phpstan.neon's own paths, stubs, and
# ignoreErrors wholesale -- level 7 is a strict superset of level 6's
# checks, not a different analysis, so every already-tuned exception
# still applies; only `level` itself is overridden below.
parameters:
    level: 7
